## Lines of attack

{{#if view.coordinator}}
- **Record every line of attack with `bin/attempts`**: where it broke, what it established anyway, what would revive it. The coordinator files workers' returns (`bin/attempts log <id> "<what happened>" --from-return -`). Before briefing work on a target, read `bin/attempts --obstructions <target>`.
- **Choosing a route on a hard target, or a write prints `AUDIT DUE`, `BUDGET REACHED` or `STALE`: load the `attack` skill** before the next attempt. A spent budget changes the attempt, not the mandate.
- **When you apply a rule tagged `(principle: <id>)`, record it** where the work is recorded: `@principle:<id> — <what it produced>`; when you skip one and give a reason anyway, `@principle-skipped:<id> — <why>`. Details: [docs/discipline/attempt-loop.md](docs/discipline/attempt-loop.md).
{{/if}}
